inithooks (2.3.6+keel6) trixie; urgency=high

  * lib/init-fence.sh: the fence no longer reports a fence it did not put up.
    A family whose nat table cannot be used, which is the normal case in an
    LXC container whose host has not loaded (ip6)table_nat, had its REDIRECT
    rule skipped with a warning, and the service then started and reported
    success with the application ports reachable over that family. The port
    is now refused in the filter table instead, inserted ahead of the rules
    the appliance firewall accepts, so what the fence promises holds by
    another means: the fence page stays reachable on its own ports, as it
    became in 2.3.6+keel1, and the application behind the fenced port does
    not answer. A port that can be neither redirected nor refused is fatal,
    with a message, because then nothing is fencing it.
  * lib/init-fence.sh: stopping removes the refusals with the redirects, so
    a stopped or failed fence leaves no port closed behind it.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:20:00 +0000

inithooks (2.3.6+keel5) trixie; urgency=high

  * declarative.py: log a deprecated field name at level "warn". It passed
    "warning", which the inithooks logger refuses, and log() caught only
    OSError, so InitLogError killed 00declarative on every boot where both
    candidate description paths exist and no description was rendered at all.
  * declarative.py: a log line can no longer stop the hook; a level the logger
    refuses goes to stderr like a log file that cannot be written.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:21:04 +0000

inithooks (2.3.6+keel4) trixie; urgency=low

  * declarative: rename security.updates to security.updates_at_first_boot,
    which is what the field controls; the old name is still read, renders the
    same conf and is reported once with its replacement.
  * declarative: add canonical() and deprecations(), the one place where a
    renamed field is translated, and validate() and render_env() read through
    them so an out of date description gets real errors instead of "unknown
    key".
  * declarative.py: report a deprecated field name on stderr and in the log.
  * tests: test_vocabulary.py freezes the vocabulary this reader accepts and,
    with KEEL_SRC pointing at the instance tooling, runs both readers over
    one document and compares their rename tables.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:09:03 +0000

inithooks (2.3.6+keel3) trixie; urgency=low

  * run: export INITHOOKS_CONF whether or not the file exists. It was
    exported only inside the test that sources it, so a hook whose job is to
    create the file got an empty path: 29preseed of the headless and qemu
    overlays failed with an ambiguous redirect on every headless first boot,
    and no hook that ran after the file was created could read it by name.
  * tests: test-run.bats, the contract between the runner and a hook,
    including the real 29preseed of the buildtasks overlay.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:57:50 +0000

inithooks (2.3.6+keel2) trixie; urgency=low

  * 00declarative: read /etc/keel/instance.yaml, and /etc/inithooks.yaml when
    that one is absent, instead of the second path only. The first appliance
    boot wrote the description to the first path and the hook read the
    second, so the description was ignored and the instance came up from an
    empty conf.
  * declarative.py: add --which, which prints the description that would be
    read, and name an ignored candidate in a warning when both exist.
  * default/inithooks: leave INITHOOKS_DECL unset by default, so the search
    happens; setting it still names a file outright.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:11:13 +0000

inithooks (2.3.6+keel1) trixie; urgency=low

  * 01ipconfig: append the static options instead of overwriting the file.
  * 01ipconfig: keep the confconsole header and the IPv6 stanza when rewriting.
  * 01ipconfig: add the IP6_CONFIG, IP6_ADDRESS, IP6_GW, IP6_DNS1 and IP6_DNS2
    preseed keys.
  * 29tagid: only reload turnkey-init-fence when it is running.
  * turnkey-init-fence: skip the REDIRECT rule when the nat table is unavailable.
  * Add the firstboot hook 00declarative: renders /etc/inithooks.conf from
    /etc/inithooks.yaml before any other hook, with bin/declarative.py
    (--check, --render, --apply) as the reader; depend on python3-yaml.
  * Add lib/ipconfig.sh, lib/tagid.sh and lib/init-fence.sh, the shell
    functions of the hooks, installed under /usr/lib/inithooks/lib.
  * Add the tests: bats for the shell hooks, pytest for the declarative
    reader, with coverage checked on every pull request.

